patch(b+'auto-thompson.md',[
('You type `(a|b)*abb` into grep and it scans a gigabyte in a second.', 'A tool such as grep -E can compile (a|b)*abb and scan input using the resulting matcher. Throughput depends on the tool, data, hardware and I/O.'),
('`.` is the union of every symbol in the alphabet.', 'In a formal wildcard notation, . can denote the union of the alphabet. Real regex engines commonly exclude newline unless a dot-all option is enabled.'),
('Backreferences like `(a+)\\1` are **not** shorthand for anything here. They take the language outside the regular languages entirely, which is why automaton-based engines refuse them (lesson 6).', 'General backreferences can express non-regular languages, such as (a+)b\\1 matching aⁿbaⁿ for n ≥ 1. Some individual backreference patterns are still regular: (a+)\\1 matches positive even-length runs of a, equivalent to (aa)+. Engines such as RE2 reject the feature syntactically rather than proving regularity separately for each pattern.'),
('```python\nfrom collections import defaultdict', 'This compact compiler accepts validated postfix expressions of literal characters and the operators ., | and *. It omits parsing, escaping, character classes and explicit ε/∅ tokens. Its global state accumulates across calls; reset delta and n before comparing independent machine sizes.\n\n```python\nfrom collections import defaultdict'),
('    return st.pop()\n\nstart, acc', '    if len(st) != 1:\n        raise ValueError("invalid postfix")\n    return st.pop()\n\nstart, acc'),
('Checked against Python\'s `re.fullmatch` on every string over {a, b} up to length 10, the two agree.', 'The audit compares this NFA with re.fullmatch on all strings over {a, b} up to length 10; that finite check supports the example but is not the general equivalence proof.'),
('GNU grep also matches with a DFA, built lazily, though it constructs it with the position-based method mentioned below rather than via Thompson\'s NFA.', 'GNU grep may select DFA, literal-search or other matching strategies depending on options and pattern features.'),
('Naive backtracking does not, which is part of the ReDoS story in lesson 6.', 'A naive recursive backtracker without a zero-progress guard may loop; practical engines commonly detect empty repetitions, although other patterns can still cause excessive backtracking.'),
('- Formal regexes have three operators (union, concatenation, star) over ∅, ε and single symbols; the rest is shorthand.', '- Formal regexes use union, concatenation and star over ∅, ε and single symbols. Many practical features are shorthand, while general backreferences add expressive power.')], 'Remove throughput claim, correct regular backreference counterexample, scope builder grammar/global state and distinguish practical empty-loop guards.',src)
